cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Belka, please cite it as below."
title: "Belka — a Belarusian language model trained from scratch"
abstract: >-
  Belka is a research project building a small Belarusian language model from scratch,
  with an auditable data-provenance model that separates original source license,
  owner-obtained research permission, and redistribution status. Research preview.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Vladymtsev
    given-names: Vadim
    affiliation: "Belka project (independent research)"
    website: "https://vadimohka.com"
    email: "vadimohkav@gmail.com"
version: "0.1.0"
date-released: "2026-06-27"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - Belarusian
  - low-resource languages
  - language model
  - from-scratch training
  - reproducibility
  - data provenance
references:
  - type: data
    title: "Belka research corpus v3b"
    notes: >-
      Mixed openly-licensed and owner-permissioned Belarusian text. Raw permissioned data
      is not redistributed. See DATA_RIGHTS_AND_PERMISSIONS.md and data_cards/corpus_v3b.md.
